{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2022-11-28 03:00:00', 'title': 'TWO THIRDS OF UK AND NORWAY NORTH SEA OIL AND GAS PRODUCTION HAS LOWER THAN AVERAGE GREENHOUSE GAS INTENSITY, NEW ANALYSIS FINDS', 'text': 'NEW S&P GLOBAL COMMODITY INSIGHTS MODEL PROVIDES UNPRECEDENTED GRANULARITY TO UNDERSTAND THE VARIATIONS IN GREENHOUSE GAS INTENSITY ON AN ASSET-TO-ASSET LEVEL LONDON , NOV. 28, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- A NEW ANALYSIS OF NORTH SEA OIL AND GAS PRODUCTION BY S&P GLOBAL COMMODITY INSIGHTS ILLUSTRATES THE DEGREE THAT GREENHOUSE GAS (GHG) INTENSITY CAN VARY FROM ONE OIL AND GAS ASSET TO THE NEXT, AND THE FACTORS THAT ULTIMATELY DETERMINE IT. THE AVERAGE GHG INTENSITY OF PRODUCTION IN THE UK AND NORWEGIAN AREAS OF THE NORTH SEA WAS 12 KILOGRAMS OF CARBON DIOXIDE EQUIVALENT PER BARREL OF OIL EQUIVALENT (KGCO2E/BOE) IN 2021.'}